---
import BaseLayout from '~/components/BaseLayout.astro';
import DocsShell from '~/components/DocsShell.astro';
import CodeBlock from '~/components/CodeBlock.astro';
import Callout from '~/components/Callout.astro';
import { SITE, VERSIONS } from '~/data/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Yeptris Python — YAML docs"
  description="The yeptris package: PyYAML-compatible YAML for Python over libyeptris — ctypes FFI, no C extension, zero compilation at install, one bulk drain per document."
>
  <DocsShell
    crumb="Yeptris — Python"
    title={`Yeptris — the YAML package v${VERSIONS.yamlPy}`}
    lede={`An FFI-based (no C extension) YAML library over libyeptris v${VERSIONS.yaml}. PyYAML-compatible semantics through ctypes — one shared library, zero compilation at install.`}
  >
    <h2 id="install">Installation</h2>
    <CodeBlock lang="bash" code={`pip install yeptris`} />
    <p>
      Self-contained wheels over ctypes: the package binds the shared
      <code>libyeptris</code> at runtime — no compiler involved, on any
      platform. A vendored per-platform library copy ships beside the
      loader; <code>YEPTRIS_LIB_PATH</code> overrides it.
    </p>

    <h2 id="usage">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="python"
      code={`import yeptris
from yeptris import yaml   # the PyYAML-compatible surface

yaml.safe_load("name: yeptris\\nrating: 10\\n")
# {'name': 'yeptris', 'rating': 10}

yaml.safe_load_all("--- 1\\n--- two\\n")   # [1, 'two']
yaml.safe_dump({"b": 2, "a": [1, "x"]})  # 'a:\\n  - 1\\n  - x\\nb: 2\\n'

yeptris.load("k: v")        # the neutral surface
yeptris.dump({"k": [1, 2]})`}
    />
    <p>
      Typing follows PyYAML&rsquo;s SafeLoader (YAML 1.1 implicit typing):
      <code>yes/no/on/off</code> booleans, <code>0x</code>/leading-0
      integers, dot-required floats, timestamps with offsets, merge keys,
      anchor identity. Constructors are ported function-for-function; every
      deliberate divergence is pinned by a test.
    </p>

    <h2 id="design">One parse, one bulk drain</h2>
    <p>
      The FFI tax is O(1) per document, never per event: the record array
      and string arena are read in two ctypes calls, then a pure-Python
      walk over the unpacked records. The record layout is ABI-pinned in
      the C header and mirrored in the package — the same seam the Ruby gem
      rides.
    </p>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="python"
      code={`docs = yeptris.load_all(stream)      # multi-document streams
                                     # [1, 'two'] for "--- 1\\n--- two\\n"

yeptris.dump({"k": [1, 2]})          # the DOM-mutation dumper:
                                     # the C emitter's sizing, style
                                     # chooser and escapes on Python trees`}
    />
    <Callout kind="note">
      <p>
        <strong>Honest perf shape:</strong> load is 28–39× pure PyYAML and
        3.8–6.1× CSafeLoader per shape. Dump is ~1.7× pure PyYAML and ~2×
        behind libyaml&rsquo;s CDumper — which walks the tree entirely in C;
        a no-C-extension design&rsquo;s ceiling is the Python walk itself.
      </p>
    </Callout>

    <h2 id="errors">Errors</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="python"
      code={`try:
    yaml.safe_load("a: [1,")
except yeptris.ParseError as e:
    ...   # the C parser's message with line/column detail`}
    />

    <h2 id="links">Where to go next</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <a href={`${SITE.githubYamlPy}`}>leptris/yeptris-py</a> — the
        canonical repository.
      </li>
      <li><a href="/docs/yeptris-getting-started">The C engine under the package</a></li>
      <li><a href="/docs/yeptris-ruby">The Ruby sibling gem</a></li>
      <li><a href="/benchmarks/yaml">The YAML benchmark campaigns</a></li>
    </ul>
  </DocsShell>
</BaseLayout>
